# In an iteration of a specialized version, an iteration guard checks that the operand of a pattern is a pristine array. If it is not, the iteration restarts in the generic version.
# The third row has an iterator method of its own assigned to it.
# So the pattern takes what that iterator yields (10, 20, 3, which adds 37), not the elements of the row (2.5, 6, 1, which would add 10).
# Fault injection, testing=AssumePristineDestructuring: the guard tests the type alone and assumes that the array is pristine.
# The elements are read in place of what the iterator yields, and nothing catches it: the iteration guard is the only safeguard.
